abstract: >-
  Canonical consolidated record of the Lambda-EG (Lambda Emergent Gravity)
  programme: the covariant scalar-tensor emergent-gravity framework (v7, with the
  a0 = 4*pi*g_crit zero-point correction), its confrontation with JADES DR4
  high-redshift data, and the geometric mu-theorem characterizing the standard
  MOND interpolating function mu(x)=x/sqrt(1+x^2) as the isotropic distribution of
  cot(theta). The acceleration scale g_crit = cH0/(4*pi^2*sqrt(3)) = 9.577e-12
  m/s^2 is derived parameter-free from De Sitter spectral geometry. Cosmology
  (CMB/FLRW) and ontology sections are forthcoming in future versions.
keywords:
  - emergent gravity
  - modified gravity
  - MOND
  - dark matter
  - baryonic Tully-Fisher relation
  - SPARC
  - JADES
  - interpolating function
  - De Sitter
  - physical cosmology
  - spacetime ontology
  - General Relativity
  - quantum field theory
